{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Entity Linking & Disambiguation Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: build an alias index from Wikipedia redirects"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "alias_to_entities = {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"jordan\": [\"Q41421 (Michael Jordan)\", \"Q810 (Jordan, country)\", \"Q254110 (Michael B. Jordan)\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"paris\":  [\"Q90 (Paris, France)\", \"Q663094 (Paris, Texas)\", \"Q55411 (Paris Hilton)\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"apple\":  [\"Q312 (Apple Inc.)\", \"Q89 (apple, fruit)\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Wikipedia alias data: ~18M (alias, entity) pairs. Download from Wikidata dumps. Store as inverted index."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: context-based disambiguation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def disambiguate(mention, context, alias_index, entity_desc):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    candidates = alias_index.get(mention.lower(), [])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if not candidates:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return None, 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    context_words = set(tokenize(context))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    best, best_score = None, -1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for entity_id in candidates:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        desc_words = set(tokenize(entity_desc[entity_id]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        union = len(context_words | desc_words)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        score = len(context_words & desc_words) / union if union else 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if score > best_score:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            best, best_score = entity_id, score"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return best, best_score"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The Jaccard overlap is a toy. Replace with cosine similarity on embeddings (see `code/main.py` step-2 for the transformer version)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: embedding-based (BLINK-style)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "encoder = SentenceTransformer(\"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def embed_mention(text, mention_span):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    start, end = mention_span"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    marked = f\"{text[:start]} [MENTION] {text[start:end]} [/MENTION] {text[end:]}\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return encoder.encode([marked], normalize_embeddings=True)[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def embed_entity(entity_id, description):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return encoder.encode([f\"{entity_id}: {description}\"], normalize_embeddings=True)[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "At index time, embed every KB entity once. At query time, embed the mention + context once, dot-product against the candidate pool, pick max."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: generative entity linking (concept)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "GENRE decodes the entity's Wikipedia title character-by-character. Constrained decoding (see lesson 20) ensures only valid titles can be output. Tight integration with a KB-backed trie. The modern descendant is REL-GEN and LLM-prompted EL with structured output."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "prompt = f\"\"\"Text: {text}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Mention: {mention}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "List the best Wikipedia title for this mention."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Respond with JSON: {{\"title\": \"...\"}}\"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Combined with a whitelist (Outlines `choice`), this is the simplest EL pipeline to ship in 2026."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: evaluate on AIDA-CoNLL"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "AIDA-CoNLL is the standard EL benchmark: 1,393 Reuters articles, 34k mentions, Wikipedia entities. Report in-KB accuracy (`P@1`) and out-of-KB NIL-detection rate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Implement the prior+context disambiguator in `code/main.py` on 10 ambiguous mentions (Paris, Jordan, Apple). Hand-label the correct entity. Measure accuracy.\n2. **Medium.** Encode 50 ambiguous mentions with a sentence transformer. Embed each candidate's description. Compare embedding-based disambiguation to Jaccard context overlap.\n3. **Hard.** Build a 1k-entity domain KB (e.g. employees + products in your company). Implement NER + EL end-to-end. Measure precision and recall on 100 held-out sentences."
      ]
    }
